{"name":"Scene Tween","title":"Scene Tween","revision":235184,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Scene_Tween","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Scene Tween is an aesthetic that emerged approximately in the early 2010s, combining elements of Kidcore and the Scene subculture. This fusion arose as mainstream culture began marketing the original Scene aesthetic towards children, much like Teenpunk with its emo-inspired imagery, but targeting an even younger audience. Scene Tween retains many of the visual elements of Scene, such as animal patterns and bright colours, but with a distinctly childish and feminine twist."},{"kind":"heading","text":"History"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In the late 2000s when the Scene emerged among teens, it began to be stripped of its original roots in order to appeal to young children of the time, with the style peaking in tween brands in the 2010s such as Justice."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"It too got deemed as a \"diva/sassy\" type of aesthetic and was more youthful and feminine much like its precursor."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Scene Tween and Scene, as mentioned above, share many similar motifs and visuals, such as:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bright colors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Animal print patterns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Animals (especially in fashion)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rainbows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Neon colors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Glitter"},{"kind":"list","text":"Peace signs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hearts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Positive messages"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Franchises"},{"kind":"list","text":"My Little Pony"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Honey Girls"},{"kind":"list","text":"Domo"},{"kind":"list","text":"Care Bears"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hello Kitty"},{"kind":"list","text":"Monster High"},{"kind":"list","text":"Littlest Pet Shop"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television and Cartoons"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Television from the Scene Tween era mainly consists of children's cartoons from said time period."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"iCarly (2007-2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Zoey 101 (2005-2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Victorious (2010-2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Make It Pop (2015-2016)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Cartoons"},{"kind":"list","text":"My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic (2010-2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Littlest Pet Shop (2012-2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hanazuki: Full of Treasures (2016-2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Strawberry Shortcake's Berry Bitty Adventures (2010-2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Popples (2015-2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rainbow Butterfly Unicorn Kitty (2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Luna Petunia (2016-2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Powerpuff Girls (1998-2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rainbow Rangers (2018-2022)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Unikitty! (2017-2020)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Toys"},{"kind":"list","text":"I Love VIP Pets Original run (2013-2017) Reboot (2020-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kittipillars/Pupillions"},{"kind":"list","text":"LOL Surprise! Tweens: Emma Emo"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Neopets (1999-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"MovieStarPlanet (2009-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fantage (2008-2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"StarSue (2006-2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stardoll (2004-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"BooniePlanet (2014)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Brands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tokidoki"},{"kind":"list","text":"So So Happy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lisa Frank"},{"kind":"list","text":"Furby"},{"kind":"list","text":"Faded Glory"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sweet n' Sassy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hot Focus"},{"kind":"list","text":"Webkinz"},{"kind":"list","text":"Twinkle Toes by Sketchers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Build-A-Bear"},{"kind":"list","text":"iScream"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/23/Scenetween.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240706143637","caption":"Scenetween","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Scenetween.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0884-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4e/Honeygirls.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240706143508","caption":"Scene Tween · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Honeygirls.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0884-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}